{
  "id": "double-dissociation",
  "term": "double dissociation",
  "definition": "A double dissociation is a pattern in which two related abilities can be disrupted separately, so that one manipulation mainly impairs the first ability while a different manipulation mainly impairs the second. In psychology, this kind of finding is used to show that the two functions depend on partly independent processes rather than a single shared one.",
